From ea6717d2725b8acd1b19837cdc6355421a94972d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SteveDeFacto <5148995+SteveDeFacto@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 10:00:44 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Guest: the launcher's CPU allocation raises the domain's
 cgroup cpu.max, and is confirmed

The measured monitor put every bundle domain in cpu.max = catalog cpuPercent (EffectivePolicy:
the bundle wins, the load request's cpu was silently ignored), so a share bigger than one
catalog CPU could not be used inside the guest. allocatedPolicy now treats CPU like the existing
RAM allocation: a load's cpu RAISES the domain's quota when it is >= the catalog cpuPercent and
<= the guest's online processors * 100, and is refused otherwise; the hashed manifest, AppID and
reports still name the catalog policy. The load answer already states the applied cpuPercent.
cpu_load_test drives the real load path (through the startDomain seam) and fails on the
pre-fix monitor, which kept cpu.max "100000 100000" when asked for 336.
wmiserve gains --app-cpu (<= 100 per VP it states), sends it as the load's cpu, refuses to serve
and destroys the domain unless the monitor answers exactly that cpuPercent, and reports it on
its load step. Needs a new guest image and shield-host.exe; the manager uses it only with
ENCLAVE_GUEST_CPU_ALLOWANCE=1.
